# MedicHub - Authentication Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Browser
    participant Frontend as Next.js Frontend
    participant Apollo as Apollo Client
    participant API as GraphQL API
    participant Auth as Auth Service
    participant Security as Security Service
    participant Prisma as Prisma ORM
    participant Redis
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    %% Registration Flow
    rect rgb(59, 130, 246, 0.1)
        Note over User,DB: Registration Flow
        User->>Frontend: Enter registration details
        Frontend->>Frontend: Client-side validation (Zod)
        Frontend->>Apollo: createAccount mutation
        Apollo->>API: GraphQL request
        API->>Auth: AccountService.createAccount()
        Auth->>Auth: Validate & hash password (Argon2)
        Auth->>Prisma: Create user
        Prisma->>DB: INSERT INTO users
        DB-->>Prisma: User created
        Auth->>Auth: Generate verification token
        Auth->>Prisma: Create token
        Prisma->>DB: INSERT INTO tokens
        Auth-->>API: User object
        API-->>Apollo: Response
        Apollo-->>Frontend: User data
        Frontend-->>User: Registration success

        Auth->>Auth: Send verification email
        Auth-->>User: Verification email sent
    end

    %% Login Flow (Without 2FA)
    rect rgb(16, 185, 129, 0.1)
        Note over User,DB: Login Flow (No 2FA)
        User->>Frontend: Enter credentials
        Frontend->>Frontend: Client-side validation
        Frontend->>Apollo: login mutation
        Apollo->>API: GraphQL request
        API->>Security: RateLimitGuard.canActivate()
        Security->>Redis: Check rate limit
        Redis-->>Security: Allowed
        API->>Auth: SessionService.login()
        Auth->>Prisma: Find user by email
        Prisma->>DB: SELECT FROM users
        DB-->>Prisma: User data
        Auth->>Auth: Verify password (Argon2)
        Auth->>Auth: Check if 2FA enabled

        alt 2FA Not Enabled
            Auth->>Auth: Create session
            Auth->>Redis: Store session
            Redis-->>Auth: Session stored
            Auth->>Prisma: Create session record
            Prisma->>DB: INSERT INTO sessions
            Auth->>Prisma: Update lastLoginAt
            Auth->>Security: Log security event
            Security->>Prisma: Create security event
            Prisma->>DB: INSERT INTO security_events
            Auth-->>API: Session + User
            API-->>Apollo: Response with cookie
            Apollo-->>Frontend: Login success
            Frontend-->>User: Redirect to dashboard
        end
    end

    %% Login Flow (With 2FA)
    rect rgb(245, 158, 11, 0.1)
        Note over User,DB: Login Flow (With 2FA)
        User->>Frontend: Enter credentials
        Frontend->>Apollo: login mutation
        Apollo->>API: GraphQL request
        API->>Auth: SessionService.login()
        Auth->>Prisma: Find user by email
        Auth->>Auth: Verify password

        alt 2FA Enabled
            Auth->>Auth: Check preferred 2FA method

            alt TOTP Method
                Auth-->>API: 2FA required (TOTP)
                API-->>Frontend: Require TOTP code
                Frontend-->>User: Show TOTP input

                User->>Frontend: Enter TOTP code
                Frontend->>Apollo: verify2FA mutation
                Apollo->>API: GraphQL request with code
                API->>Auth: TwoFactorMethodService.verify()
                Auth->>Prisma: Get authentication method
                Prisma->>DB: SELECT FROM authentication_methods
                Auth->>Auth: Verify TOTP code (OTPAuth)
                Auth->>Auth: Valid, create session
                Auth->>Redis: Store session
                Auth->>Prisma: Update method lastUsedAt
                Auth->>Prisma: Create session (is2FAVerified: true)
                Auth-->>API: Session + User
                API-->>Frontend: Login success
                Frontend-->>User: Redirect to dashboard
            else OTP (Email/SMS) Method
                Auth->>Auth: Generate OTP code
                Auth->>Redis: Store OTP with TTL
                Auth-->>API: OTP sent
                API-->>Frontend: Check email/SMS
                Frontend-->>User: Show OTP input

                User->>Frontend: Enter OTP code
                Frontend->>Apollo: verify2FA mutation
                Apollo->>API: GraphQL request with OTP
                API->>Auth: TwoFactorMethodService.verify()
                Auth->>Redis: Get stored OTP
                Redis-->>Auth: OTP value
                Auth->>Auth: Compare codes
                Auth->>Redis: Delete OTP
                Auth->>Auth: Create session
                Auth->>Redis: Store session
                Auth->>Prisma: Create session record
                Auth-->>API: Session + User
                API-->>Frontend: Login success
                Frontend-->>User: Redirect to dashboard
            else WebAuthn Method
                Auth-->>API: WebAuthn challenge
                API-->>Frontend: Challenge data
                Frontend->>Browser: navigator.credentials.get()
                Browser-->>User: Show biometric/key prompt
                User->>Browser: Authenticate (Face ID/Key)
                Browser-->>Frontend: Assertion response
                Frontend->>Apollo: completeWebAuthnAuthentication mutation
                Apollo->>API: GraphQL with assertion
                API->>Auth: WebAuthnService.verifyAuthentication()
                Auth->>Prisma: Get credential
                Auth->>Auth: Verify assertion (@simplewebauthn)
                Auth->>Prisma: Update counter, lastUsedAt
                Auth->>Auth: Create session
                Auth->>Redis: Store session
                Auth-->>API: Session + User
                API-->>Frontend: Login success
                Frontend-->>User: Redirect to dashboard
            end
        end
    end

    %% Failed Login (Rate Limit & Account Lock)
    rect rgb(220, 38, 38, 0.1)
        Note over User,DB: Failed Login (Rate Limit)
        User->>Frontend: Enter wrong credentials
        Frontend->>Apollo: login mutation
        Apollo->>API: GraphQL request
        API->>Security: RateLimitGuard.canActivate()
        Security->>Redis: Increment attempt counter

        alt Rate Limit Exceeded
            Security-->>API: RateLimitException (429)
            API-->>Frontend: Too many requests
            Frontend-->>User: Please wait X seconds
        else Within Rate Limit
            API->>Auth: SessionService.login()
            Auth->>Prisma: Find user
            Auth->>Auth: Verify password
            Auth->>Auth: Password incorrect
            Auth->>Security: AccountLockService.recordFailedAttempt()
            Security->>Prisma: Get account locks
            Security->>Security: Increment failed attempts

            alt Failed Attempts >= Threshold
                Security->>Prisma: Create account lock
                Prisma->>DB: INSERT INTO account_locks
                Security->>Redis: Set lock flag
                Security->>Auth: Send lockout notification
                Security-->>API: Account locked
                API-->>Frontend: Account locked
                Frontend-->>User: Account locked for X minutes
            else Within Threshold
                Security->>Prisma: Log security event
                Auth-->>API: Invalid credentials
                API-->>Frontend: Login failed
                Frontend-->>User: Invalid credentials
            end
        end
    end

    %% Password Reset Flow
    rect rgb(124, 58, 237, 0.1)
        Note over User,DB: Password Reset Flow
        User->>Frontend: Click "Forgot Password"
        Frontend->>Apollo: resetPassword mutation (email)
        Apollo->>API: GraphQL request
        API->>Security: RateLimitGuard (reset password)
        API->>Auth: RecoveryService.resetPassword()
        Auth->>Prisma: Find user by email
        Auth->>Auth: Generate reset token
        Auth->>Prisma: Create token (PASSWORD_RESET)
        Prisma->>DB: INSERT INTO tokens
        Auth->>Auth: Send reset email with link
        Auth-->>API: Email sent
        API-->>Frontend: Success
        Frontend-->>User: Check your email

        Note over User,DB: User clicks email link
        User->>Frontend: Click reset link (with token)
        Frontend-->>User: Show new password form
        User->>Frontend: Enter new password
        Frontend->>Apollo: newPassword mutation (token, password)
        Apollo->>API: GraphQL request
        API->>Auth: RecoveryService.newPassword()
        Auth->>Prisma: Find token
        Prisma->>DB: SELECT FROM tokens WHERE token = ?
        Auth->>Auth: Validate token (not expired, not used)
        Auth->>Auth: Hash new password (Argon2)
        Auth->>Prisma: Update user password
        Prisma->>DB: UPDATE users SET password = ?
        Auth->>Prisma: Mark token as used
        Auth->>Prisma: Revoke all sessions
        Auth->>Redis: Delete all sessions
        Auth->>Security: Log password changed event
        Auth-->>API: Password changed
        API-->>Frontend: Success
        Frontend-->>User: Redirect to login
    end

    %% Session Validation (Per Request)
    rect rgb(34, 197, 94, 0.1)
        Note over User,DB: Authenticated Request
        User->>Frontend: Navigate to protected page
        Frontend->>Apollo: GraphQL query (with cookie)
        Apollo->>API: Request with session cookie
        API->>Auth: GqlAuthGuard.canActivate()
        Auth->>Redis: Get session by cookie ID
        Redis-->>Auth: Session data

        alt Session Valid
            Auth->>Prisma: Get user by session userId
            Prisma->>DB: SELECT FROM users
            DB-->>Prisma: User data
            Auth->>Auth: Attach user to request context
            Auth-->>API: Authorized
            API->>API: Execute resolver
            API-->>Frontend: Response
            Frontend-->>User: Show page
        else Session Invalid/Expired
            Auth-->>API: UnauthorizedException (401)
            API-->>Frontend: Unauthorized
            Frontend-->>User: Redirect to login
        end
    end

    %% Logout Flow
    rect rgb(107, 114, 128, 0.1)
        Note over User,DB: Logout Flow
        User->>Frontend: Click logout
        Frontend->>Apollo: logout mutation
        Apollo->>API: GraphQL request (with cookie)
        API->>Auth: SessionService.logout()
        Auth->>Redis: Delete session
        Redis-->>Auth: Session removed
        Auth->>Prisma: Update session (revokedAt)
        Prisma->>DB: UPDATE sessions SET revokedAt = NOW()
        Auth->>Security: Log logout event
        Auth-->>API: Logged out
        API-->>Frontend: Clear cookie
        Frontend-->>User: Redirect to login
    end
```

## Authentication Flow Components

### 1. Registration Flow
**Steps**:
1. User submits registration form
2. Client-side validation (Zod schema)
3. Password hashing with Argon2
4. User creation in database
5. Email verification token generation
6. Verification email dispatch
7. Return user object

**Security Measures**:
- Password strength validation (min 8 chars)
- Email format validation
- Unique email/phone constraint
- Verification token (15 min expiry)

### 2. Login Flow (No 2FA)
**Steps**:
1. Rate limit check (Redis)
2. User lookup by email
3. Password verification (Argon2)
4. 2FA status check
5. Session creation (Redis + DB)
6. Security event logging
7. Return session cookie

**Rate Limiting**:
- 5 login attempts per 15 minutes
- Tracked by IP address
- Redis ZSET sliding window

### 3. Login Flow (With 2FA)
**TOTP Flow**:
1. Credentials verified
2. Return 2FA required response
3. User enters TOTP code
4. Code verification (30-second window)
5. Session creation with 2FA verified flag
6. Redirect to dashboard

**OTP Flow (Email/SMS)**:
1. Credentials verified
2. Generate 6-digit OTP
3. Store OTP in Redis (5 min TTL)
4. Send OTP via email/SMS
5. User enters OTP
6. Verify against Redis
7. Session creation

**WebAuthn Flow**:
1. Credentials verified
2. Generate challenge
3. Browser prompts for biometric/key
4. User authenticates
5. Verify assertion
6. Update credential counter
7. Session creation

### 4. Failed Login Handling
**Rate Limiting**:
- Check rate limit before processing
- Throw 429 if exceeded
- Return retry-after header

**Account Lockout**:
- Track failed attempts per user
- Lock after N attempts (default: 5)
- Temporary lock (30 minutes)
- Notification email sent
- Progressive delays (50ms → 1s)

**Security Events**:
- LOG all failed attempts
- HIGH severity for multiple failures
- CRITICAL for brute force detection
- Include IP, user agent, timestamp

### 5. Password Reset Flow
**Request Reset**:
1. User provides email
2. Rate limit check (3 per 3 hours)
3. Generate unique token
4. Store token in DB (15 min expiry)
5. Send email with reset link

**Complete Reset**:
1. User clicks link with token
2. Validate token (exists, not expired, not used)
3. User enters new password
4. Hash new password
5. Update user password
6. Mark token as used
7. Revoke all sessions
8. Log security event

**Security**:
- Token single-use only
- Short expiration (15 min)
- Session revocation on password change
- Email notification

### 6. Session Validation
**Per-Request**:
1. Extract session cookie
2. Lookup session in Redis (fast)
3. Validate session (not expired, not revoked)
4. Fetch user from DB if needed
5. Attach user to request context
6. Update lastUsedAt timestamp

**Session Metadata**:
- Device fingerprint
- IP address, location
- User agent, browser, OS
- 2FA verification status
- Risk score

### 7. Logout Flow
**Steps**:
1. Delete session from Redis
2. Mark session as revoked in DB (revokedAt)
3. Log logout security event
4. Clear session cookie
5. Redirect to login

**Options**:
- Single session logout (current)
- All sessions logout (account-wide)
- Remote session removal (from session list)

## Key Security Features

### Multi-Factor Authentication
- Support for multiple 2FA methods simultaneously
- User-selectable preferred method
- Backup codes for recovery
- Device trust management

### Rate Limiting
Per-endpoint rate limits:
- Login: 5 / 15 min
- Password reset: 3 / 3 hours
- 2FA verification: 5 / 5 min
- Email verification: 3 / 15 min

### Account Protection
- Account lockout after failed attempts
- Progressive delays on failures
- Automatic unlock after timeout
- Email notifications on security events

### Session Management
- Redis for fast session lookup
- DB for persistent session history
- Session expiration (configurable)
- Device tracking and management
- Session revocation support

### Risk Scoring
Real-time calculation based on:
- New device detection
- Unusual location
- Failed attempt history
- Time of day
- IP reputation

### Audit Trail
Comprehensive logging:
- All login attempts (success/failure)
- 2FA setup and verification
- Password changes
- Session creation/revocation
- Account locks
- Suspicious activities
